{title: Watchman for the House}
{subtitle: Ezekiel 3:17–21}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Son of man I speak to [Gm7]you
I made you a watchman true
[Eb]For the house of Israel [Bb]now
Hear my [F]word and let [Bb]it show
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
To the wicked I have [Gm7]said
You will surely die instead
If [Eb]you stay silent in the dark
His [F]blood is on your mark
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Warn them now before [Eb]they fall
[Bb]Speak the word [Eb]to stand them [Gm]tall
If they re[Eb]fuse to turn a[F]way
Their guilt remains for al[Bb]ways
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]If you warn and they do not change
The [Gm7]wicked path is their range
They [Eb]die in guilt before your eyes
But [F]you have saved your life
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Warn them now be[Eb]fore they fall
[Bb]Speak the word to [Eb]stand them tall
[Gm]If they refuse to [Eb]turn away
Their [F]guilt remains for al[Bb]ways
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Even [Gm]righteous may turn a[Eb]side
Place a [Bb]stumbling block to [F]hide
If you [Gm]fail to warn the [Eb]just
Their good [F]deeds are turned to dust
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Warn the righteous not [Eb]to sin
[Bb]He lives because he did lis[Eb]ten
[Gm]You have saved your own [Bb]life [Eb][Bb]
{end_of_verse}
